WEBVTT

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:04.560
Excuse me. We were asked 
to bring these here.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.560
Civilians aren't allowed in here-

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.950
Nobody move.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.270
I don't know what rebel group you're with,

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:18.030
but do you really think you're
 going to get away with this?

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.660
We are the RLF.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.530
What are you after?

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.920
True Freedom and Equality.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:28.750
You-

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.650
I'm sorry you didn't get to fight with us.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.270
This base is under our control.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.520
Why... What are you doing?

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.440
Please! Join our fight!

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.820
I can't.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.370
I don't fight humans!

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.330
Very well then.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:08.560
Do you really think you can 
change the world like this?

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:09.590
Of course.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.750
America's top secret research...

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:24.400
Natalie!

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:01.450
Come in! This is the 
Argos Test Flight hangar!

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.450
Come in!

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.040
Damn it! Nobody's picking up!

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.650
It's me! Lt. Takamura!

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.250
Open the door!

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.050
I came under attack at the command center.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:19.540
You're kidding!

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.610
What's happening out there?

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:23.430
This is a UN base!

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:26.120
Prepare the TSFs for launch.

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:27.430
Where are the Eishi?

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:30.810
VG and Stella are getting 
their enhancement suits on.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.640
Yuuya and Tarisa aren't back yet.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.290
All TSFs prepare to launch!

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.190
TSFs are sitting ducks unless they're moving.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:48.740
<b>The Future Tears Open</b>

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.570
Shutting down Enzyme injection.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.660
Injection stopped.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.250
D-Do you think...

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.220
Do you think you're going 
to get away with this?

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:09.570
Check.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:37.670
Connection complete.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.650
Opening direct line to the master.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:45.760
Damn it!

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:47.850
Reporting.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.680
We have successfully captured Yukon base.

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:53.700
This is all as the Lord wished.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.230
<b>Local Time 15:45</b>

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.450
Look, it's Ensign Bridges!

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.820
Ensign Bridges is back!

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.750
Yuuya!

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.560
You're safe?

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.820
Bridges!

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:19.500
Cryska!

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:22.120
Did you see Inia somewhere?

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.880
No... What about you?

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.490
Sergeant Lowell.

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:28.650
Launch all TSFs.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:30.480
I'm heading for the Royal Guard hangar.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.340
Get those TSFs fueled up!

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:41.820
What are you doing, Tarisa?

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.680
Activate all Idar Flight TSFs.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:53.180
Head to hangar B01 immediately.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:56.290
But Ensign Barchenowa is missing!

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:57.290
What?

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:08.700
I don't care. Our priority is 
securing Ensign Sestina's safety.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.510
Roger.

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:16.770
Connecting to combat area datalink.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.020
This is strange. The information 
hasn't been updated.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.020
It's me.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:25.780
All TSFs are to launch 
as soon as they're ready.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:28.220
Keep a close eye on your surroundings 
and see what's going on.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:33.580
Their highest priority was the security 
squad, since they had real bullets.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:37.080
We've only got mock combat bullets here.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.680
Why'd they attack us?

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:41.580
Lt. Takamura, it's me!

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:44.840
I'm requesting one of your spare machines.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.340
Spare?

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:48.730
Spare... You mean...

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:50.500
You've got one, right? Right there!

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:54.350
Do we have time for this? Give it to me!

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.320
That's US Military property!

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:00.190
Both of the Strike Eagles 
are ready to go, right?

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:04.360
Lt. Takamura, I'd like to use one as well.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.440
Lieutenant, the enemy is approaching.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:10.610
Argos 4 to all units.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:14.980
The combat area datalink we're 
looking at is all fake data.

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:18.250
Short range communications are 
possible so set it to local mode.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:22.750
It's no good. We set it to local 
but we still can't see the enemy.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:27.130
Sergeant Lowell, boot up both Strike Eagles.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.300
Are you serious?

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.050
I'll take responsibility!

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.560
Are you not ready yet? Hurry!

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:42.100
I know! I'm going as fast as I can!

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.600
Then go faster!

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:47.860
What's got you so pissed off?

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:53.030
Natalie died!

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.450
And she was a terrorist!

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:02.960
But she was shot because she tried 
to tell us what was going on!

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:04.210
Damn it!

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:06.680
What are they thinking?

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.480
I don't understand!

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:12.170
We've just got to accept the fate we've been dealt.

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.570
I know that!

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:18.500
Okay then. Otherwise, 
you'll be the next to die.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:20.440
Hey, Tarisa.

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:23.010
Well...

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:28.020
We know for sure that Natalie lost 
her life trying to save us, right?

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:31.360
Isn't that enough?

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:36.320
They're close! A distance 
of 12000, to the southeast!

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:39.130
Get the empty tanks out of here!

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:40.790
The Active can come later!

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:43.210
Your first priority is the Shiranui Type 2!

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:46.860
It's me.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:51.810
I'm transferring the new attack target 
that was in our sealed orders.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.380
These coordinates...

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:58.160
We're not supposed to be here.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:00.120
Kill any witnesses.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.310
All units operational. Beginning mission.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.370
The handling on this TSF isn't very tight.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:12.540
But...

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:16.260
Ensign Cryska Barchenowa. Launching.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:20.080
Cryska, what are you doing?

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:22.440
I'll hold off the enemy.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:24.080
You're kidding me!

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.210
Undo the connectors locking me in.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:27.940
You don't have any weapons!

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:29.570
You'll just get killed if 
you go out there alone!

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:32.360
I'll use the Full Boost. The 
mechanics need to get out of here.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.090
Everyone, get out of here!

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:42.850
She's insane.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.110
So it's self-defense now.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:09:59.960
New TSFs detected.

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:01.380
Eight of them.

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:04.120
This is Cui Yifei. Ready to go.

00:10:04.690 --> 00:10:05.620
Launching!

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:06.870
Oww...

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:16.670
It takes forever to get used 
to a brand new flight suit.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:23.970
Now let me have some fun!

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:26.980
You okay, Vincent?

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:28.900
I guess so.

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:31.480
Okay, you and Tarisa are set to go!

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:35.380
I just repainted the thing too.

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:39.130
Listen, those long swords were 
borrowed from the Royal Guard.

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:41.240
Take good care of them.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:41.990
Roger.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:48.620
Here we go!

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:52.080
First one down!

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:58.090
Looks like the party's already started.

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:07.090
The comms center is already 
under our control.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:10.440
We've finished hacking the 
satellite network as well.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.080
Then it's going well.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:17.360
The US and Soviets must be pissed off 
they've lost their eyes and ears.

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:22.020
The security squads are taken care 
of as well. We can relax a little.

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:26.370
By the way, your sister did a good job.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:28.240
I see.

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:31.810
Who is it that's controlling 
you from behind the scenes?

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:34.000
Is it America? The African Union?

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:36.200
Or Oceania?

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:38.840
This is Commander Rogofsky of the USSR.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:41.130
This is him, huh?

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.000
The base commander is in 
a coma in the hospital.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.540
Heartwick is missing.

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:48.140
He's the one in charge here.

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:51.390
We answer only to the Lord.

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:56.080
We've come to punish you for 
disobeying his commands.

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:57.900
You're from the Christian Allegiance?

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:01.540
I'd prefer you weren't so rude, Major.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:06.480
Don't pick unneccessary fights, and 
it makes everything go smoother.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:07.520
Yes sir.

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:10.660
We'll follow the plan here as well.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.580
I look forward to seeing you again.

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:17.130
Major, there are some issues.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:17.920
What?

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:20.840
We've lost track of the Infinities.

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.550
They left the base before 
we began our attack.

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:26.370
The hyenas.

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.160
Good for them.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:29.460
A-And...

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:31.610
The Idar Flight is fleeing as well.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:34.420
We have an entire company following them...

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:38.290
Get two more to the border and surround them!

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:39.970
Don't let them get away.

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:40.760
Yes sir.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:43.940
But what are they doing?

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:46.240
That was too fast for them to be running.

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:49.970
Someone contacted them 
from within this building.

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:51.330
It was probably them.

00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:53.020
Honestly...

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:56.620
Even God's plans don't work out so well.

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:59.200
I'll go deal with them.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:02.420
I'll be back soon. Please take of things here.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:07.840
Major! Our forces have encountered 
the enemy near the west side hangars!

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:09.720
We're being pushed back.

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:12.100
How many do they have compared to us?

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:13.490
Five enemies.

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:16.560
We have eight TSFs on autopilot,

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.020
and six have already been shot down.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:20.940
By the Test Flights?

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:23.780
They're not supposed to have live ammunition!

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:25.730
What Flight?

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:29.620
The XFJ project. Argos Test Flight.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:33.450
Interesting. This must be fate.

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:36.480
Call our forces back.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:38.960
We can make use of them 
later. Let them alone!

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.500
Argos 3 to all units. Here I am!

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:49.410
Huh?

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:52.260
They're withdrawing...

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:57.530
There are two assault cannons 
with live ammunition.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:59.350
You take one.

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:01.800
I'm impressed.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:03.360
I didn't think you could 
take one down like that.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.210
Use everything you can.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:07.860
That's how the USSR fights.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.260
All TSFs are to find weapons they can use.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:13.870
Keep an eye out for traps.

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:20.260
We'll split into two ad-hoc 
Flights with our seven TSFs.

00:14:20.260 --> 00:14:23.340
I'll take charge. Second will be Lt. Cui.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:26.800
Sounds fair for an outsider.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.470
So what do we do now?

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.530
We'll move to urban combat 
training grounds A207.

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:34.800
That can be our base for 
information gathering.

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:37.980
I see. It's got a lot of obstructions 
so it's good for defense.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:39.760
Sergeant Lowell.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:42.820
The mechanics are to abandon 
the hangar immediately.

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:46.480
Finish wiping any classified data 
and get to the bomb shelters.

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:47.940
Roger.

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:50.160
All mechanics are present and accounted for.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:53.300
Mr. Heinemann had a meeting at HQ today.

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:53.870
I see.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:58.360
Which means he must be 
in a Boerning shelter.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.220
I hope he's safe...

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:03.010
Lt. Takamura.

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:05.760
I'm returning to my own Flight.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:07.540
What are you talking about, dummy?

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:10.290
We can't give a captain's unit to the East!

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:14.020
Request denied. It's dangerous 
to go alone right now.

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:15.940
I...

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.880
I have to go!

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:20.100
Please!

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:24.770
Yui.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.940
The enemy already knows we're here.

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:31.530
Even if we head to the combat grounds 
we need to be ready for an ambush.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:34.880
If we go to the Idar Flight hangar first 
and circle around, we can avoid it.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:38.020
And there's a chance Soviet 
reinforcements will be there as well.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.220
It's not a bad idea.

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:54.970
This is Yukon base.

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:57.460
We're under attack by an unknown force.

00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:00.400
Repeat. This is Yukon base.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.010
We're under attack by an unknown force.

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:03.010
This voice...

00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:11.360
The Laser Class BETA practice warning?

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:14.260
For the next 36 hours,

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:16.090
the area in a 300 kilometer 
radius is a no-flight zone?

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:18.580
Fake information spread by the terrorists.

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:22.250
It makes it psychologically more 
difficult to use any airplanes.

00:16:22.570 --> 00:16:23.600
Yeah.

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:25.080
Lt. Takamura.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:30.260
There's something I learned as I dispatched 
several soldiers on my way out of the base.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:32.590
The enemy is not military trained.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:36.930
They're either a paramilitary group 
or trained refugee volunteers.

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:46.310
Also, until we split up Lt. Dahl was alive.

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.410
He's likely still hiding 
in the Command center.

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:54.520
I have a suggestion...

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:58.250
We should go north and head 
to the USSR's B01 hangar.

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:00.280
It has propellant and live ammunition.

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:03.480
That's inside the Soviet part of Yukon Base.

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:07.290
We're not going to be surrounded by Idar 
Flight and forced to give up our TSFs, are we?

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:10.170
Please don't get the wrong idea, Lt. Cui.

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:14.300
All Idar TSFs are on standby 
in another location.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.550
No...

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:18.290
Then Inia...

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:21.050
Is piloting the Terminator alone?

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:24.260
Calm down. She has the 
other Idar TSFs with her.

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:25.660
But...

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:27.250
Lt. Sandek.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:32.660
It's also possible for us to request support 
and resupply at the US Anchorage base...

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:34.820
No, I wouldn't be so sure.

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:41.250
That might be what gets you arrested 
and your TSFs confiscated.

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:42.930
What do you mean?

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:45.120
Whoever's behind this attack...

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.970
There's a good chance they're American.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:00.180
Damn it!

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:02.180
Don't.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.780
Throw down your weapon and come out.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:08.690
We are the RLF.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.780
We don't want to kill unneccessarily.

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:14.380
My name is Mariem Zarner.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:16.450
I'm fighting for the Turkish Refugees.

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:23.480
Lt. Ibrahim Dahl of the Turkish Army.

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:27.090
Ibrahim?

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:28.490
Dahl...

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.490
He can't be...

00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:32.660
The hero of Rhodes?

00:18:32.660 --> 00:18:35.590
The man who defied orders 
multiple times for the refugees?

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:37.590
Captain Dahl!

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:40.090
I'm one of the ones you saved.

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:43.480
You're a hero, you saved 
the lives of many refugees.

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:45.780
There's no reason for us to fight.

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:51.370
Take this. I'm going to talk to him.

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:54.110
Wait. It's dangerous!

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:56.130
Captain!

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:58.330
I'm going over there alone.

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:00.220
Please let me talk to you.

00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:04.370
I'll be back.

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.420
Run, Idar 1!

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:26.930
Cryska! I'm scared! I'm scared!

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:35.290
A new enemy? From where?

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:47.200
They're gone?

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:48.580
Why?

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:52.540
Why... don't you kill me?

00:19:57.850 --> 00:19:59.640
Are you sure about this, Captain?

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:00.840
Couldn't just leave her.

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.460
That's our next target.

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:07.350
Now let's get back to our original mission.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:12.850
America is a country that will take 
any measure to ensure its security.

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:17.360
And yet still a terrorist attack 
of this size is occuring in Alaska.

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:21.240
You mean the government 
allowed this to happen?

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:28.050
Playing the role of victim to advance its own 
goals has been an American trick for a long time.

00:20:28.050 --> 00:20:30.370
They've done it many, many times before.

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:32.640
You're right, it's suspicious.

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.870
Like the Infinities being 
sent here all of a sudden.

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:39.380
It's dangerous to rely 
on America at this point.

00:20:39.770 --> 00:20:41.160
But Lieutenant.

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:43.740
The USSR is the shield of North America.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:45.380
What's the point of causing them trouble?

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:48.420
It doesn't matter now.

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:50.140
So what do we do, Yui?

00:20:54.490 --> 00:20:59.650
Argos 3 and 4 have a long range. We'll send 
them to Anchorage base in US territory.

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:04.400
The rest of us will stay here and gather 
information at combat grounds A207.

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:06.760
Afterwards we'll head to B01.

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:08.160
There, we'll load up on live ammunition.

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:11.120
Wait! We're splitting our forces?

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:15.920
With communications cut off right now, we 
need to let someone know what's going on.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:21.810
The terrorists may have 
acquired as many as 108 TSFs.

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:23.720
We won't be able to defeat them with seven.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:27.980
We'll call for help from 
outside and guide them in.

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:29.520
I see.

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:32.180
So you're betting on both sides, then.

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:34.340
We have no objections.

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:36.310
Same here.

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:40.690
Okay, let's get going then.

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:45.080
Tarisa, don't kick too much butt 
and tear down the whole base, okay?

00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:47.070
We won't have anywhere to come back to.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:50.320
Dummy. And you'd better not make 
any rest stops on the way there!

00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:52.760
It'll be fine, Tarisa.

00:21:52.760 --> 00:21:53.920
I'll keep an eye on him.

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:55.830
Scary, scary.

00:21:56.320 --> 00:21:58.720
Okay, you take care of it here then.

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:02.210
Don't die, you guys...

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:06.840
Enemies are approaching. Unknown number.

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:10.840
Everyone hurry to combat grounds A207.

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:13.600
Place sonic sensors as soon as you get there.

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:16.100
Our priority is to find out 
what exactly's going on.

00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:17.770
Mission start.

00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:21.850
Gisele, it's me.

00:22:21.850 --> 00:22:22.610
Major...

00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:26.990
Those guys are good. They 
took out six TSFs unarmed.

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:29.080
Keep your distance.

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:32.320
We'll slowly tear them apart 
with guided rounds. Got it?

00:22:32.690 --> 00:22:34.020
Roger.

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:07.940
Releasing pilot safety function.

00:24:07.940 --> 00:24:09.690
Let's go, partner!

00:24:09.690 --> 00:24:14.360
So they've got the ultimate 
anti-air system, huh?

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:18.090
Captain, the answer you never found...

00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:24.440
<b>Untainted Revenge</b>

00:24:18.090 --> 00:24:20.530
It seems I've found it.

00:24:20.530 --> 00:24:22.540
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:22.930 --> 00:24:24.490
Untainted Revenge.
